Description: Python interface to the ZFS utilities (zfs and zpool)
 libzfseasy wraps the zfs and zpool command line tools as Python objects:
 typed datasets, snapshots and bookmarks, property handling with sources, and
 one command class per zfs subcommand, including streaming send and receive.
 .
 It uses only the Python standard library and runs the zfs and zpool binaries
 found on PATH (or named by the ZFS_CMD and ZPOOL_CMD environment variables).
 .
 This package is released together with zfsbackup, which depends on it.

