Description: Automated ZFS snapshots, retention and remote backup over mutual TLS
 zfsbackup is a daemon that snapshots ZFS datasets on a schedule, prunes the
 snapshots with tiered retention rules, and replicates them to other hosts
 with incremental zfs send and receive over HTTPS with mutual TLS
 authentication and pinned certificates. One daemon can be a backup client, a
 backup server, or both.
 .
 The configuration lives in a SQLite database managed with zfsbackup-config.
 The service is neither enabled nor started on installation: import a
 configuration, enroll the destinations, then run
 "systemctl enable --now zfsbackup". See /usr/share/doc/zfsbackup/README.md.
 .
 The daemon uses the development server of werkzeug and overrides internals
 of werkzeug, urllib3 and simple-websocket: werkzeug and simple-websocket are
 therefore limited to the minor series this version was tested with
 (werkzeug 3.1, simple-websocket 1.1) and sqlalchemy to 2.0 and 2.1; the
 other libraries are bounded to their current major version.
